  "text": "POV-Ray 2.2 is built, installed, and working. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Sourced the archives** — POV-Ray 2.2 source (1994) isn't on the official GitHub (history starts at v3.7). I found the original distribution files on the Internet Archive's `mbcd9495` (MikroBitti CD 94/95) collection:\n- `povsrc-2.zip` — the C source (38 `.C` files + headers, confirmed `#define POV_RAY_VERSION \"2.2\"`)\n- `povdoc-2.zip` — the standard include library (`shapes.inc`, `colors.inc`, `textures.inc`, etc.)\n\n**Built it** at `/app/povray-2.2`:\n- Extracted source to `/app/povray-2.2/SOURCE/` and machine-specific Unix code in `MACHINE/UNIX/`\n- Set up a build directory: lowercased the K&R-era `.C`/`.H` filenames, created `config.h` (from `unixconf.h`), and used the Unix `makefile`\n- Compiled with `gcc` — built cleanly (only warnings about K&R-style implicit declarations, no errors)\n\n**Installed and provisioned**:\n- Binary → `/usr/local/bin/povray`\n- Include library → `/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include/` (matches the `+L` path in the test command)\n\n**Sanity check passes** — the exact command renders `/app/deps/illum1.pov` and reports full statistics (91,599 rays traced, sphere/plane/quadric intersections, shadow/reflection/refraction counts), exit code 0. I also verified a real render produces a valid 30KB TGA image.",
