        "input": {
          "description": "Find povray 2.2 source download",
          "prompt": "I need to find a downloadable source code archive for POV-Ray version 2.2 (also known as \"Persistence of Vision Raytracer\" version 2.2, released around 1993-1994). This is a very old version of the POV-Ray raytracer written in C.\n\nThe source was historically distributed as ZIP archives, commonly named things like:\n- povsrc22.zip\n- pvsrc22.zip  \n- povray22.zip\n- pvsource.zip\n- povunix.scr (Unix source)\n\nPlease search the internet and try to find any working, downloadable URL for the POV-Ray 2.2 source code. Try these sources and report back which ones actually work (return a downloadable file):\n1. Internet Archive (archive.org) - search for CD images or software collections containing POV-Ray 2.2 source, e.g. the \"PEGASUS\" collection, Walnut Creek CD-ROM images, Hobbes OS/2 archive, cd.textfiles.com mirrors\n2. GitHub repositories that might mirror the old 2.2 source (search for files named like \"frame.c\", \"povray.c\", \"lighting.c\", \"render.c\" or directories named \"source\" with version 2.2)\n3. Old FTP mirror archives\n4. Any other working source\n\nFor each candidate URL you find, attempt to verify it actually contains POV-Ray 2.2 source (the source would contain files like frame.c, povray.c, tokenize.c, parse.c, render.c, lighting.c, and a file stating version 2.2). \n\nReport back the BEST working download URL(s) you find, the exact filename, and what format it is in (.zip, .tar.gz, directory tree, etc.). Do NOT actually download large files - just identify and verify the correct URLs. Prioritize accuracy over speed."
        }
      }
    },
