    {
      "ts": 1786351461449,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Excellent! I found the structure. The files exist on the FTP server but most CDX entries are redirects. The key file is the Unix source `povuni_s.tgz`. Let me find actual archived copies with real content (status 200)."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786351461449,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_956f4e4fa24a4e45a6dd8b6a",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /app\n# Look at the actual 1996 directory listing to find real filenames\necho \"=== 1996 povray ftp listing ===\"\ncurl -sL --max-time 30 \"https://web.archive.org/web/19961223111443/http://www.povray.org:80/ftp/pub/povray/\" 2>&1 | sed 's/<[^>]*>//g' | grep -iE \"pov|src|uni|2\\.2|tgz|zip|tar\" | head -40\n"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786351462200,
      "type": "tool_result",
      "call_id": "call_956f4e4fa24a4e45a6dd8b6a",
      "output": {
        "ok": {
          "content": "=== 1996 povray ftp listing ===\n  __wm.wombat(\"http://www.povray.org:80/ftp/pub/povray/\",\"19961223111443\",\"https://web.archive.org/\",\"web\",\"https://web-static.archive.org/_static/\",\nIndex of /ftp/pub/povray\nFTP.POVRAY.ORG - OFFICIAL POV-Ray RAYTRACER SITE.\nSee Official-3.0/ for all official POV-Ray source and binaries.\n\n[exit code: 0]"
        }
      },
      "duration_ms": 750,
      "speculated": false
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786351462200,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_278c16d6b55848248f8c1d6e",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /app\n# Search for actual 200-status captures of unix source archives across all mirrors\necho \"=== CDX: povuni_s.tgz with 200 status ===\"\ncurl -sL --max-time 40 \"https://web.archive.org/cdx/search/cdx?url=povuni_s.tgz&matchType=suffix&filter=statuscode:200&filter=mimetype:application/(gzip|x-gzip|octet-stream|zip|x-tar)&limit=30&output=json&collapse=urlkey\" 2>&1 | head -40\n"
        }
      }
    },
