      "ts": 1786351585812,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "All captures are 303 redirects (the FTP→HTTPS redirect), never the actual 200 content. The Wayback Machine only saved the redirect HTML, not the binary file itself. Let me try the `POVSRC.ZIP` and also check if the file is available directly now, plus check archive.org items."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786351585812,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_35891dcabb29459e8f5f67aa",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /app\n# Try downloading POVSRC.TAR.Z directly following the redirect chain on the live FTP server\n# The captures redirect to a different path. Let me see where they go.\necho \"=== Follow redirect for POVSRC.TAR.Z ===\"\ncurl -sL --max-time 30 \"https://web.archive.org/web/20260630010327/https://ftp.povray.org/pub/povray/Old-Versions/Official-2.2/POVSRC.TAR.Z\" 2>&1 | sed 's/<[^>]*>//g' | grep -iE \"location|redirect|301|302|303|moved|href\" | head -10\necho \"=== Direct attempt at live HTTPS ===\"\ncurl -sIL --max-time 20 \"https://www.povray.org/pub/povray/Old-Versions/Official-2.2/POVSRC.TAR.Z\" 2>&1 | grep -iE \"HTTP/|location|content-type|content-length\" | head -10\n"
        }
      }
    },
