      "output": {
        "ok": {
          "content": "=== README2.2 via wayback ===\nThis directory contains the official POV-Ray 2.2 archives created by the \nPOV-Ray Development Team.  The original location of these files on internet\nis alfred.ccs.carleton.ca (134.117.1.1).  Begining with this release, this \nsite will no longer retain any versions of POV-Ray other than the most recent\nversion.  We ask that any sites which mirror this official site and any\nBBS or other service which redistributes POV-Ray to please remove any \nearlier versions of our official files from circulation.  Note that we do \nallow unofficial versions of POV-Ray to be distributed under the rules \noutlined in POVLEGAL.DOC.  Please retain only the most recent available\nversion of these custom versions as well.  For example a custom compile for\nXYZ-Workstation version 2.1 should only be retained if no 2.2 version is\navailable.  An important provision of our rules is that custom versions \nmust be clearly marked as unofficial.  We ask sysops and site managers to \ndo what they can to clearly distinguish the official archives obtained here \nfrom custom versions submited by others.\n\n=== KNOWNBUGS.DOC via wayback ===\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <title>Wayback Machine</title>\n    <script>\n    /*\n    @licstart  The following is the entire license notice for the JavaScript code in this page.\n\n    Copyright (C) 2020 Internet Archive\n\n    The JavaScript code in this page is free software: you can\n    redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU Affero\n    General Public License as published by the Free Software\n    Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or (at your option)\n    any later version.  The code is distributed WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;\n\n[exit code: 0]"
