          "command": "cd /app\n# pov_20190813 is \"POV RayTracer 3.6.1a\". linuxbrew/homebrew are modern. \n# Let me check the Walnut Creek Linux Games CD more carefully - it's from 1999, likely has povray 2.x or 3.0 source.\n# I'd need to download the ISO. But first, let me check the \"mbcd9495\" (MikroBitti) and CHIP CDs which are shareware compilations.\n# \n# Better idea: Let me check what version is on these CDs by looking at their file listings.\n# But these are ISOs. Let me instead try to find the source on a Git-hosted vintage mirror.\n# \n# Let me search GitHub for the EXACT distinctive filename \"atmosph.c\" or \"radiosi.c\" which are POV-Ray specific\n# Wait - those are 3.x. For 2.2, distinctive files: bndbox.c, chunk.c, disp.c, digit.c\n# Let me try GitHub search API with these (unauth might work for some)\necho \"=== github search repos: 'pov-ray' OR 'povray' older code ===\"\n# Check beeejorgensen/povray - could be a teacher's repo with old source\ncurl -sL --max-time 20 \"https://api.github.com/repos/beejjorgensen/povray/git/trees/master?recursive=1\" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '\"path\": \"[^\"]*\"' | head -30\n"
        }
      }
