        {
          "block_id": "blk_080df3af679c8cb7088bd42b",
          "content_digest": "sha256:a7130a0e5dfdfab049b021b2a636dc63467b0111feecc1afe3264a6622fedab0",
          "content": "{\"ok\":{\"content\":\"=== FILE_ID.DIZ ===\\nThis is the source code in highly \\r\\nportible C for the Persistence of \\r\\nVision Ray Tracer POV-Ray version \\r\\n2.2. It also include machine \\r\\nspecific source for all platforms \\r\\nexcept Macintosh. (Mac users see \\r\\nPOVSRC.SEA)  Create your own \\\\POVRAY2\\r\\ndirectory and un-zip this file using \\r\\nthe -d option to insure that the \\r\\nproper sub-directories are created. \\r\\nOther files are needed.  See \\r\\nPOVINF.DOC from this library for more \\r\\ninformation.\\r\\n\\n=== WHATSNEW.DOC (first lines) ===\\n    What's New in POV-Ray 2.2\\r\\n    --------------------------\\r\\n\\r\\n    This bug-fix release adds no new features but fixes the following\\r\\n    bugs from version 2.1.\\r\\n\\r\\n  - Fixed problem with declared material_maps or declared objects with\\r\\n    material_maps (yet again)\\r\\n  - Eliminated unnecessary tu\\n[… middle elided during compaction — re-run the tool for the full output …]\\nec numbering.  Upper\\r\\n    left pixel is 1,1.  Fixed -ec bug.\\r\\n  - Fixed three bezier patch bugs which caused lock-ups, missing reflection,\\r\\n=== version define in frame.h ===\\n*  Forum.  The latest version of POV-Ray may be found there as well.\\r\\n* This program is based on the popular DKB raytracer version 2.12.\\r\\n#define POV_RAY_VERSION \\\"2.2\\\"\\r\\n#define DISTRIBUTION_MESSAGE_1 \\\"This is an unofficial version compiled by:\\\"\\r\\n#define DISTRIBUTION_MESSAGE_3 \\\"The POV-Ray Team is not responsible for supporting this version.\\\"\\r\\n/* If compiler version is undefined, then make it 'u' for unknown */\\r\\n\\n[exit code: 0]\\n\\ntip: this looks like a symbol/dependency lookup — graph_query answers it directly (op=definitions|references|callees|callers|imports|importers|neighbors), precise and cheaper than a text scan.\"}}"
        },
        {
          "block_id": "blk_ca16bdf703a8e3e4c179a96c",
          "content_digest": "sha256:ddbdf6b083541ab19214042321753e3efc607c67793372ec44ba81ade60aa2a4",
          "content": "{\"ok\":{\"content\":\"=== MACHINE/UNIX contents ===\\ntotal 108\\ndrwxrwxrwx. 2 root root 16384 Sep 26  1993 .\\ndrwxrwxrwx. 8 root root    98 Aug 10 08:58 ..\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  1832 Aug  6  1993 GCC.C\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  6252 Aug  6  1993 GCCCONF.H\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  6228 Aug  6  1993 RS6CONF.H\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  1852 Oct  3  1993 UNIX.C\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root   996 Nov 11  1992 UNIX.CAT\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  4657 Sep 30  1993 UNIX.DOC\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  3486 Oct  9  1993 UNIX.MAK\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  6296 Aug  6  1993 UNIXCONF.H\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  3275 Nov 11  1992 XPOV.ICN\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root 16174 Aug  6  1993 XWIN.C\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root 17623 Aug  6  1993 XWINDOWS.C\\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  3618 Oct  9  1993 XWINDOWS.MAK\\n\\n=== UNIX.DOC ===\\nThis file contains the d\\n[… middle elided during compaction — re-run the tool for the full output …]\\n directed to Chris Cason\\r\\non Compuserve via mail or in the POV source section of GRAPHDEV. (currently 8).\\r\\n\\r\\nHe will continue to enhance this code and test it other machines.\\r\\nIf you had to make any modifications to get it to compile, please let him know\\r\\nso that he may update the source accordingly. This particularly applies to\\r\\nthe build files. By doing so, you will be helping others.\\r\\n\\r\\nYou may like to check the POV section of GRAPHDEV on Compuserve to see if there\\r\\nare updated X files, which may occur from time to time.\\r\\nTry scanning for the keyword XWINDOWS.\\r\\n\\r\\nExpect to find a significantly enhanced X version in the near future.\\r\\n(Sometime in late 1993 or early 1994). This will include a Motif shell.\\r\\n\\r\\nChris Cason.\\r\\nCIS:100032,1644\\r\\nInternet:100032.1644@compuserve.com\\n[exit code: 0]\"}}"
