    {
      "ts": 1786352396359,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The lowercase loop used `.C` (uppercase) in basename but the actual extension on disk is `.C`. The issue is that on this case-sensitive FS, the files have `.C` extension. My loop `basename \"$f\" .C` should work... Let me check why POVRAY.c is mixed-case."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786352396359,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_a5b983f6d1fc4d16b7210309",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /app/povray-2.2/build\n# The file is POVRAY.c (uppercase name). basename issue. Let me redo cleanly with proper lowercase of the whole name\nrm -f *.c *.h unix.c config.h makefile\nfor f in ../SOURCE/*.C; do\n  base=$(basename \"$f\" .C | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z')\n  cp \"$f\" \"$base.c\"\ndone\nfor f in ../SOURCE/*.H; do\n  base=$(basename \"$f\" .H | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z')\n  cp \"$f\" \"$base.h\"\ndone\ncp ../MACHINE/UNIX/UNIX.C unix.c\ncp ../MACHINE/UNIX/UNIXCONF.H config.h\ncp ../MACHINE/UNIX/UNIX.MAK makefile\necho \"=== check key files ===\"\nls povray.c unix.c config.h makefile\necho \"=== all .c ===\"\nls *.c | tr '\\n' ' '"
        }
      }
    },
