    {
      "ts": 1786352447519,
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Now let me set up the proper POV-Ray directory structure. The test command uses `+L/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include` as the library path. Let me create that structure and install the binary."
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786352447519,
      "type": "tool_start",
      "call": {
        "call_id": "call_fc0eadbfb46c433c995ea932",
        "name": "bash",
        "input": {
          "command": "cd /app/povray-2.2\n# Create the povdoc/include directory structure that the test command references\nmkdir -p povdoc/include\n# Copy all include files (lowercase them for unix)\ncd /tmp/povdoc/INCLUDE\nfor f in *.INC; do\n  base=$(basename \"$f\" .INC | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z')\n  cp \"$f\" \"/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include/$base.inc\"\ndone\n# Also copy the GIF files (image maps might be referenced)\nfor g in *.GIF; do\n  base=$(basename \"$g\" .GIF | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z')\n  cp \"$g\" \"/app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include/$base.gif\"\ndone\necho \"=== povdoc/include contents ===\"\nls -la /app/povray-2.2/povdoc/include/"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786352447554,
      "type": "tool_result",
      "call_id": "call_fc0eadbfb46c433c995ea932",
      "output": {
        "ok": {
          "content": "=== povdoc/include contents ===\ntotal 216\ndrwxrwxrwx. 2 root root 16384 Aug 10 09:00 .\ndrwxrwxrwx. 3 root root    21 Aug 10 09:00 ..\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root 15584 Aug 10 09:00 chars.inc\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  8705 Aug 10 09:00 colors.inc\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root   702 Aug 10 09:00 fov.inc\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root   398 Aug 10 09:00 ior.inc\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root 39211 Aug 10 09:00 rough.gif\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  3387 Aug 10 09:00 shapes.inc\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  4768 Aug 10 09:00 shapes2.inc\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root 11327 Aug 10 09:00 shapesq.inc\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root 60161 Aug 10 09:00 stones.inc\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root  5080 Aug 10 09:00 test.gif\n-rw-rw-rw-. 1 root root 32455 Aug 10 09:00 textures.inc\n\n[exit code: 0]\n\nnote: this cd'd to `/tmp/povdoc/INCLUDE`, outside the session root `/app`. Only work under the session root is collected when the turn finishes — every other tool is confined to it, so edits under `/tmp/povdoc/INCLUDE` are invisible to the file tools, to this turn's diff, and to verification. graph_query and the grep/glob code-map footers index only this root, so it isn't covered by the code graph either. To work on that tree, re-root the session on it (run stella from it)."
        }
