      "ts": 1786352517864,
      "type": "file_change",
      "path": "povray-2.2/FILE_ID.DIZ",
      "kind": "created",
      "added": 13,
      "removed": 0,
      "diff": "@@ -1,0 +1,13 @@\n+This is the source code in highly \n+portible C for the Persistence of \n+Vision Ray Tracer POV-Ray version \n+2.2. It also include machine \n+specific source for all platforms \n+except Macintosh. (Mac users see \n+POVSRC.SEA)  Create your own \\POVRAY2\n+directory and un-zip this file using \n+the -d option to insure that the \n+proper sub-directories are created. \n+Other files are needed.  See \n+POVINF.DOC from this library for more \n+information.\n"
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786352517871,
      "type": "file_change",
      "path": "povray-2.2/KNOWNBUG.DOC",
      "kind": "created",
      "added": 20,
      "removed": 0,
      "diff": "@@ -1,0 +1,20 @@\n+\n+                  Persistence of Vision Raytracer\n+                           Version 2.2\n+                        Known Bug Information\n+                  -------------------------------\n+\n+The only verified bug that we have found but not fixed in POV-Ray 2.2\n+is that you may not nest a tiles texture within a tiles texture.\n+The POV-Ray Team is working on the problem but decided to not delay \n+this release further.  See WHATSNEW.DOC for the bugs we did fix.\n+\n+   If you have any questions about POV-Ray, please contact\n+\n+     Chris Young\n+     [POV-Team Coordinator]\n+\n+     CIS: 76702,1655\n+     Internet: 76702.1655@compuserve.com\n+\n+\n"
    },
    {
      "ts": 1786352517879,
      "type": "file_change",
      "path": "povray-2.2/MACHINE/ACORN/ARM.C",
      "kind": "created",
      "added": 30,
      "removed": 0,
      "diff": "@@ -1,0 +1,30 @@\n+#include <stdio.h>\n+\n+#include \"bbc.h\"\n+#include \"sprite.h\"\n+\n+extern char DisplayFormat;\n+extern char PaletteOption;\n+\n+static struct\n+{\n+    int red, green, blue;\n+} colour_error;\n+\n+void display_init(int width, int height)\n+{\n+\n+}\n+\n+void display_finished(void)\n+{\n+}\n+\n+void display_close(void)\n+{\n+}\n+\n+void display_plot(int x, int y, unsigned char Red, unsigned char Green, unsigned char Blue)\n+{\n+    printf(\"*%d,%d,%d,%d,%d\\n\", x, y, Red, Green, Blue);\n+}\n"
    },
